.TH GUARA 1 "2026-09-19" "guara 0.1.0" "Guará manual"
.SH NAME
guara \- filesystem search, tracking, and light security signals
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B guara
[\fIPATTERN\fR] [\fIROOTS\fR]... [\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.br
.B guara
\fICOMMAND\fR [\fIARGS\fR]...
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B guara
searches file names and file contents in one pass, attaches lightweight
security signals to every hit, and never mutates the filesystem unless an
explicit flag asks it to. Running
.B guara
without a subcommand is the same as
.BR "guara search" .
.PP
Statistics and warnings go to standard error, so
.B \-\-json
on standard output stays machine-readable. Exit codes: 0 when at least one hit
was printed (or a non-search command succeeded), 1 when a search found nothing,
2 for usage or configuration errors, and 3 when the run finished with partial
filesystem errors.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B search
Search names and contents. This is the default command.
.TP
.B config
Print the configuration file path and the effective settings as JSON.
.TP
.B index
Build or update the persistent SQLite index.
.B "index status"
reports the path count, database path, and last update time.
.TP
.B reindex
Rebuild the index from scratch for the given roots.
.TP
.B history
Print recent local search queries.
.TP
.B serve
Watch the roots and update the index as files change until interrupted.
.BI \-\-socket [= PATH ]
also listens for the tray and palette IPC protocol on a local Unix socket.
.TP
.B tui
Browse results in a terminal UI: incremental filter, preview pane, open with
.BR $EDITOR ,
and re-run the heuristics on the selected path. Without a terminal it prints
the results like
.BR search .
.SH SEARCH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-e ", " \-\-regex
Treat the pattern as a regular expression.
.TP
.BR \-i ", " \-\-ignore\-case
Case-insensitive matching.
.TP
.BR \-w ", " \-\-word
Match whole words only.
.TP
.BI \-t ", " \-\-term " PATTERN"
Add another pattern. Multiple patterns default to AND.
.TP
.B \-\-or
Match any pattern instead of all of them.
.TP
.BI \-\-context " N"
Print
.I N
lines before and after each content match.
.TP
.BI \-\-max\-count " N"
Stop after
.I N
hits (0 means unlimited).
.TP
.BI \-\-max\-depth " N"
Limit directory depth. 1 means only top-level entries.
.TP
.B \-\-follow\-symlinks
Follow symlinks. The default is not to follow them.
.TP
.BI \-\-ext " EXT"
Restrict to a file extension. Repeatable.
.TP
.BI \-\-min\-size " SIZE" ", " \-\-max\-size " SIZE"
Filter by size in bytes, or with a
.BR k ,
.B m
or
.B g
suffix (for example
.BR 10M ).
.TP
.BI \-\-after " DATE" ", " \-\-before " DATE"
Filter by modification date,
.IR YYYY\-MM\-DD .
.TP
.B \-\-binary
Include binary files in content search. They are skipped by default.
.TP
.BR \-\-json ", " \-\-csv ", " \-\-html
Emit one JSON object per hit, CSV, or a self-contained HTML report.
.TP
.BR \-\-compact ", " \-\-table
One line per file, or a tabular mode.
.TP
.BI \-\-color " WHEN"
.I always
,
.IR never ,
or
.IR auto .
.B NO_COLOR
is honored.
.TP
.B \-\-deep\-scan
Opt in to the deep scanners, which need a matching Cargo feature at build time
and a backend flag
.RB ( \-\-clamd\-socket ,
.BR \-\-rules\-dir ,
.BR \-\-hash\-db ).
.TP
.B \-\-quarantine
Move flagged files into
.B \-\-quarantine\-dir
and record them in a manifest. Report-only by default; never deletes in place.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-index
Always walk the filesystem instead of answering from the index.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I <config_dir>/guara/config.toml
Optional TOML configuration. CLI flags win over the file, which wins over the
built-in defaults.
.TP
.I <data_dir>/guara/index.db
Persistent index (SQLite).
.TP
.I <data_dir>/guara/guara.sock
Local IPC socket used by
.BR "guara serve \-\-socket" .
.TP
.I <config_dir>/guara/tray.json
Tray preferences: auto-start (off by default), pinned scopes, recent queries.
.SH SECURITY MODEL
The always-on heuristics report, they do not act: quarantine requires both
.B \-\-quarantine
and a destination directory, and files are moved, never deleted. Guará offers no
real-time protection, cannot guarantee detection, and performs no network
reputation lookup or telemetry. See the threat model in the documentation.
.SH SEE ALSO
Documentation in the repository:
